 "why_these_families": "The rat-D class is where E-Q9's falsifier literal reading fired: fixed HOLDS at the 1,134 dyadic family points (T2: fixed hold <=> dd dyadic, 0 violations in the 306,773-fraction census). E-Q9 swept them one-row-per-family; nothing full-traced their trajectories, and the class was never moth-ordered. They are also the cleanest standing-instrument test bed: every family's outcome at the family point is pinned by census arithmetic, so the pipeline's honesty is checkable per family.",
 "open_variables_closed_here": {
  "pool": "stable && rat.cls==D over the E-Q9 census bounds (n<=252, dd<=253, gcd=1) — 1,134 families, registered census order (dd asc, n asc). Pool composition (census arithmetic, pre-run): dd=1: 252 families; dd in {2,4,8,16,32,64,128}: 126 each (252+126*7=1,134, all dyadic as T2 demands).",
  "near_arm_split_of_the_pool": "irrNear = double(n/dd + SQRT2*2^-52): 379 of the 1,134 are F-INV (fixed BLIND — Q32.32 door cannot see the sqrt2*2^-20 S-unit step — while float sees the ~1-ulp step and moves); 755 are degenerate (sigma >= 4: the irrational step rounds back below half-ulp; near run == rat run); 0 non-degenerate D. The F-INV membership of each family is census-determined, so post-selection the expected near class per selected family is pinned BEFORE any kernel run.",
  "float_direction_in_finv": "Pre-run arithmetic over all 379 pool F-INV cells: float pressure sign +1 (UP) in 379/379, -1 (DOWN) in 0, 0 in 0. The float move is dd*sigma2 - n >= dd*SQRT2*2^-52 > 0 after the sum's rounding — UP always in this pool.",
  "far_arm_directions": "irrFar = sqrt2: both planes move together (byte-identical, E-Q9 E6); direction DOWN -1 iff sigma = n/dd > sqrt2. Pre-run arithmetic: 953 of the 1,134 pool families have sigma > sqrt2 (expected DOWN count in 16 moth-chosen families: 16*953/1134 = 13.45). These are B-class both-move events, NOT the artifact: no fixed-hold is involved.",
  "moth_budget": "MAX 2 jobs (lane-tight, tighter than the client's E-X5 module cap of 4). Job 1 primary at shots=1024. Reserve job 2 spent ONLY if job 1's von Neumann output < 256 bits (the selection needs ~118 bits = log2 C(1134,16); 256 is margin); then VN runs over the CONCATENATED raw streams in order. If job 1 fails: receipt the FAIL, spend job 2 once, else stop. Unreachable/failed API => honest FAIL verdict file, zero deep trace, everything committed AS RUN.",
  "key_and_archive_law": "MOTH_KEY only ever read at runtime by the client (moth_client.mjs, VERBATIM copy of pt-exoj/experiments/moth_bits.mjs with a provenance header — the live-job-proven wave-41 client); never printed, logged, or committed. Raw bits, VN bits, and the whitened seed block are archived OUTSIDE the repo at /home/z/my-project/scripts/42b-moth-bits/ (key-free) and enter the repo ONLY as sha256 pins. no_leak_scan runs on every file the receipt touches before it is written."
 },
 "whitener": {
  "input": "raw_bits: the job's canonical measurement expansion (distinct 8-bit outcomes sorted ascending, each expanded by its count, MSB-first; moth_client.mjs extractBits — receipted E-D3 shape). Top-20 truncation is carried, not hidden: captured bits < shots*8, receipted as bits_len.",
  "step_1_von_neumann": "consecutive PAIRS (b0,b1): (0,1)->emit 0; (1,0)->emit 1; (0,0),(1,1)->emit nothing. Removes the 0.63/0.37 balance bias; output rate ~2p(1-p) ~= 0.47 of pairs.",
  "step_2_byte_pack": "vn_bits MSB-first into bytes; trailing pad bits (0..7) are ZERO and pad_len is receipted.",
  "step_3_counter_stream": "block_c = SHA-256( u32be(c) || vn_bytes ) for c = 0,1,2,...; the whitened stream is block_0 || block_1 || ... consumed MSB-first. The 256-bit SEED is block_0; whitened_seed_sha256 = SHA-256(block_0). Entropy honesty: the stream beyond the VN output (~1,000 bits expected) is a deterministic SHA-256 PRF EXTENSION of the moth entropy — entropy-bounded by the VN output, receipted as such, replayable byte-exact from the archived raw bits (--bits-from-file).",
